# 6 Improvements: Multi-Feature LSTM, Best-Run Ranking, Data Leakage Fix, Stop Button, History Chart

## Proposed Changes

### 1. Multi-Feature LSTM (OHLCV + Technical Indicators)

#### [MODIFY] [preprocessor.py](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py)
- Update [prepare_lstm_data()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py#156-207) to use **10 features** instead of only close price:
  - `close`, `open`, `high`, `low`, `volume`
  - `rsi_14`, `macd`, `bb_middle`, `atr_14`, `daily_return`
- Use `MinMaxScaler` per-feature (fit only on **training portion** — fixes data leakage)
- Use [create_feature_sequences()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py#111-127) (already exists) which outputs shape [(samples, seq_len, n_features)](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/backtest/engine.py#23-167)

#### [MODIFY] [trainer.py](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/models/trainer.py)
- Update [train_lstm()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/models/trainer.py#36-69) to call technical indicators and pass multi-feature data
- Update [_predict_lstm()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/models/trainer.py#205-214) to prepare multi-feature input for prediction

---

### 2. Data Leakage Fix

#### [MODIFY] [preprocessor.py](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py)
- In [prepare_lstm_data()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py#156-207): **fit scaler only on training data**, then transform val/test
- Current bug: [normalize_prices(prices, fit=True)](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/preprocessor.py#81-89) fits on ALL data before splitting

---

### 3. Best-Run Ranking (Direction Accuracy + MAPE)

#### [MODIFY] [storage.py](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/data/storage.py)
- Change [get_best_training_run()](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/api/routes/predictions.py#237-251) SQL query to rank by **composite score**:
  ```
  score = 0.6 * (100 - avg_directional_accuracy) + 0.4 * avg_mape
  ```
  Lower = better. Weights Direction Accuracy 60%, MAPE 40%.

---

### 4. Stop Auto-Tune Button

#### [MODIFY] [Prediction.jsx](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/frontend/src/pages/Prediction.jsx)
- Add `autoTuneCancelRef = useRef(false)` to track cancellation
- Add a **Stop button** (red) that sets `autoTuneCancelRef.current = true`
- Check the ref at each loop iteration — break if cancelled

---

### 5. Training History Chart

#### [MODIFY] [Prediction.jsx](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/frontend/src/pages/Prediction.jsx)
- After Auto-Tune ends, fetch [getTrainingHistory(symbol)](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/frontend/src/api/client.js#37-38) from API
- Display a line chart (using existing [PlotChart](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/frontend/src/components/PlotChart.jsx#4-40) component) with:
  - X: Run number / timestamp
  - Y: MAPE + Direction Accuracy per run
- Show inside the Auto-Tune Log panel

---

## Verification Plan

### Automated Tests
- Run backend server, trigger training via API
- Verify LSTM input shape is [(samples, seq_len, 10)](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/backtest/engine.py#23-167) instead of [(samples, seq_len, 1)](file:///d:/AI/fund_predition/backend/backtest/engine.py#23-167)
- Verify scaler is fit only on training data
- Verify best-run ranking considers both Direction Accuracy and MAPE

### Manual Verification
- Click Auto-Tune → observe log panel → verify multi-feature training works
- Click Stop button mid-loop → verify it stops
- After auto-tune, verify history chart appears with trend data
